;; a corpus bin/validate judges typeflow on. :role is the honest label —
;; :in-sample was learned from, :held-out was judged after the rules were
;; written, :blind was never read before its first score was recorded.
;; JS: the oracle is a shadow-cljs release log (closure.log) plus Closure's
;; extern property names (externs.edn, bin/oracle-js). The sources are a git
;; worktree of defnet at 92270f9^, the last commit whose viewer still had
;; its 42 :infer-warnings.
{:name "defnet-viewer-old"
 :root "~/.cache/sift/corpora/defnet-viewer-old/src/defnet/viewer"
 ;; recreate: git -C ~/GitHub/defnet archive "92270f9^" src/defnet/viewer
 ;;           | tar -x -C ~/.cache/sift/corpora/defnet-viewer-old
 :oracle "~/.cache/sift/oracles/defnet-viewer-old"
 ;; first scores (2026-08-27): the pre-existing model, 262 predicted for 42
 ;; (P 0.16 R 1.00); with Closure's externs, 62 (P 0.68); with string-require
 ;; aliases as js, 50 (P 0.84 R 1.00) — where it stands. Adding npm property
 ;; names reclaimed the 8 and lost 14: recorded in bin/oracle-js, not used.
 :role :held-out}
